                       "label":  "77",
                       "number":  77,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "When Apollonius heard of it, he drew up three thousand cavalry and a large force of infantry. He marched toward Azotus as though he were going on through, but at the same time he was advancing into the plain, because he had such a large number of cavalry to rely on.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "78",
                       "number":  78,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Jonathan pursued him toward Azotus, and the armies engaged in battle.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "79",
                       "number":  79,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Apollonius, however, had left a thousand cavalry in hiding behind them.",
