                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "80",
                       "number":  80,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Jonathan discovered that there was an ambush behind him; his army was surrounded. From morning until evening they showered his troops with arrows.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "81",
                       "number":  81,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "But his troops held their ground, as Jonathan had commanded, while the enemy’s horses became tired out.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "82",
                       "number":  82,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Then Simon brought forward his force, and engaged the phalanx in battle. Since the cavalry were exhausted, the phalanx was crushed by him and fled,",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "83",
                       "number":  83,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "while the cavalry too were scattered over the plain. They fled to Azotus and entered Beth-dagon, the temple of their idol, to save themselves.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "84",
                       "number":  84,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "But Jonathan burned and plundered Azotus with its neighboring towns, and destroyed by fire both the temple of Dagon and those who had taken refuge in it.",
